      "targeted_symptom": "additional_requirement_1",
      "patient_response": "Um, well... I guess it’s not entirely new. I really hate admitting this, because I always wanted to be the perfect student, and I really did try my best! But, yeah... even back in elementary school, I had some of these same issues. \n\nMy teachers would always write on my report cards that I was bright, which was really sweet of them, but... they'd also write that I was constantly losing my worksheets. Or that I’d rush through the directions and miss things. And I guess I talked out of turn a lot, too. I just got so eager to participate, you know? I really wasn't trying to be disruptive or disrespectful! \n\nAnd, um... my desk was always just a complete disaster. It was so messy that I literally couldn't find my assignments when it was time to hand them in. It’s so embarrassing to look back on, honestly. I hope that doesn't make me sound like I was an awful kid. I promise I was a good kid, I just struggled to keep it all together! Does that help answer your question, or did you mean more recently?",
